    {
      "id": "claim_e3c00ef8916e42d299ef4610155dabf0",
      "statement": "tests/receiver-double-accept.test.mjs (PR #117) is a regression-guard file that `npm test` runs via `node --no-warnings --test \\\"tests/*.test.mjs\\\"` (bringing the repo's regression-guard file count from 42 to 43). It pins the onAccept double-accept re-entrancy guard: a second Accept click landing in the same frame as the first (before Svelte re-renders the button away, while the entry is already Processing) previously passed the bare null guard and sent a second EVENT_RECEIVER_ACCEPT, re-initializing the chunk/stats maps so the sender's persistent ACCEPT handler fired sendNextChunk() concurrently and the same chunk went on the wire twice (double-counting receivedSize, so the fully delivered file was marked Success with duplicated bytes or rejected as oversized). The combined guard `if (!receivingFile || receivingFile.status !== FileStatus.WaitingAccept) return;` bails before the ACCEPT send, also covers dead-channel entries bounced to Pending, and does not short-circuit the metadata-failure reject branch — the test pins all of it with a pre-fix control (two ACCEPTs), post-fix no-op proofs (one ACCEPT, chunk map not recreated, a dead-channel Pending entry stays Pending), a metadata-failure entry still rejecting, and static regex guards on the real onAccept.",
